.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH fleetring-cert-init 1  FleetRing "FleetRing manual"
.SH NAME
fleetring\-cert\-init \- Creates the authority: `ca.crt` and `ca.key` in the directory
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBfleetring cert init\fR [\fB\-\-ttl\fR] [\fB\-\-log\-format\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-\-color\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fB\-\-fleet\fR> <\fB\-\-dir\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Creates the authority: `ca.crt` and `ca.key` in the directory
.PP
Keep `ca.key` off every node; it is the one secret that issues certificates.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-fleet\fR \fI<FLEET>\fR
The fleet\*(Aqs name, which every certificate the authority issues names
.TP
\fB\-\-dir\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
The directory to write into; created if missing
.TP
\fB\-\-ttl\fR \fI<TTL>\fR
How long the authority\*(Aqs certificate lasts: `<n>d`, `<n>h`, `<n>m`, or `<n>s`

Ten years by default.
.TP
\fB\-\-log\-format\fR \fI<LOG_FORMAT>\fR
Writes log lines as `text` or `json`

Overrides `FLEETRING_LOG_FORMAT` and the configuration file\*(Aqs `[log] format`.
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Prints the result and errors only

No progress, notes, warnings or override warnings. A command with no result then prints nothing.
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR \fI<COLOR>\fR [default: auto]
When to colour log lines and the picker

`auto` colours on a terminal unless `NO_COLOR` is set or `TERM` is `dumb`; `always` and `never` do as they say.
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
auto: On a terminal, unless `NO_COLOR` is set or `TERM` is `dumb`
.IP \(bu 2
always: Always, even into a pipe or a file
.IP \(bu 2
never: Never
.RE
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
